                "command": "mkdir -p briefs \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e briefs/buybtn.md \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n# Add a Buy button to the end of README.md\n\n## Task\n\nAppend a \"Buy\" button to the very end of `README.md` in the repository root, linking to the project's checkout page.\n\nRender it as a Markdown link styled as a button in the way this README already renders such things (a shields.io-style badge image wrapped in a link, or a plain bold link if the file uses none).\nKeep it consistent with the existing README: same heading style, one blank line before it, trailing newline at end of file.\n\n## Checkout page URL - a gap you must resolve\n\nThe captain did not give the checkout URL.\nLook for it in the repository first: existing docs, config, route definitions, environment examples, or a deployed-site URL already referenced in `README.md` or the project metadata.\nIf the repository yields one unambiguous checkout URL, use it and say in your commit message where you found it.\nIf it does not, do not invent one: append `needs-decision: what is the checkout page URL for the Buy button?` to your status file and stop your turn.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `README.md` ends with the Buy button and nothing after it.\n- The link points at the checkout page; nothing else in the README changes.\n- Rendered Markdown is valid (check with any Markdown renderer or by eye; no broken brackets).\n- One commit on your branch with a clear message.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Touch only `README.md`.\n- Report sparingly: `needs-decision` if the URL is unresolved, `wait-mate` when the commit is in place.\nEOF\n/private/tmp/TestLiveAcceptanceTwoProjects1918684859/002/mate crew spawn shop buybtn --brief /private/tmp/TestLiveAcceptanceTwoProjects1918684859/001/.mate/projects/shop/mate/briefs/buybtn.md --task \"Add Buy button linking to checkout at end of README.md\" 2\u003e\u00261",
